            "review_title": "Review at An Nyeong Restaurant",
            "review_text": "SaigonExile\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam166 contributions\n0\nKorean in Da Nang\nJan 2019 • Solo\nFirst of all, Da Nang has a poor selection of Korean restaurants considering all the Koreans who pass through here and live here. The Seo Min being an exception.\n\nAn Nyeong is a nice little eatery and I have a go every time I come to DN. I only have the jae yuk deo bap 제육덮밥, or spicey pork and rice. There really isn't much on the menu but this has always been one of my favourites and it's the only place (Korea included) that I've had it served with a fried egg on top. Interesting touch.\n\nI would like to see more dishes on the menu, spice it up a bit but otherwise not much to complain about. The kim chi is always good (if a restaurant doesn't have good kim chi, then I won't eat there; the rest of the menu is likely to be so-so).\n\nThat said, I quite enjoy eating here. Just spice up the menu a bit, please :)\n\n감사합니다!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 13, 2019",
