            "review_text": "Olga L\nChiang Mai, Thailand162 contributions\n0\nVery disappointing\nApr 2017 • Couples\nFirst , to be fair, I would like to state the positive aspects to our experience here. The staff, 2 young Vietnamese girls were very attentive and kind. They made us feel welcome and they are the only positive to this establishment.\n\nMy husband had the Pork Cutlet with Rice. The dish came with a tiny serving of rice, unheard of for this dish. He had to ask for more, and he did get a decent bowl full of rice. BUT BUT he had to ask for it. He was not charged extra for this. The meat itself was not sensational by any means.\n\nI had a noodle in a tomato sauce. It was a small serving and tasted canned.\n\nThere was no \"love\" in the food given. Why not a side dish of kimchi? ....just a little something to make us sit up and take notice.\n\nWe continue to walk by this restaurant as we are staying here for 26 days and every time it is empty, that is no surprise. Early evening - empty. Late evening - empty. There is a good reason for this.\n\nA suggestion to the owner would be: in the case of pork cutlet - you cannot serve this dish with such a small serving of rice.\n\nWe were totally disatisfied and will not go back there, at least not during this visit.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 12, 2017\n현상 나\nDear Olga L\nThank you for your advice. We will consider your suggestion. But we don't use tomato sauce into Noodle and do you want how big dish? I think you have to check your tongue and personality. We can't agree with you.\nNonetheless, We are so sorry for you feel like this.\n\nKind Regards,\nNa Hyun Sang\nRead more\nWritten April 14, 2017\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
